From: OpsReplay Bookworm backport
Subject: Restrict LANGUAGE catalog paths for all programs

Adapted from Avinal Kumar's upstream v7 proposal for BZ 17142:
https://inbox.sourceware.org/libc-alpha/20261012112453.47383-1-avinal.xlvii@gmail.com/
The proposal is under review, not a released GNU or Debian fix.
Only its production lookup change is backported to Debian 2.36-9+deb12u14.

--- a/intl/dcigettext.c
+++ b/intl/dcigettext.c
@@ -687,4 +687,4 @@
-	  /* When this is a SUID binary we must not allow accessing files
-	     outside the dedicated directories.  */
-	  if (ENABLE_SECURE && IS_PATH_WITH_DIR (single_locale))
-	    /* Ingore this entry.  */
+	  /* Do not allow accessing files outside the dedicated
+	     directories.  */
+	  if (IS_PATH_WITH_DIR (single_locale)
+	      || strcmp (single_locale, "..") == 0)
